# Ektelo — contact form email delivery
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in ONE of the two providers below.
# .env.local is gitignored. Never commit real keys.
#
# Confirm what the running app picked up:  curl http://localhost:3000/api/contact
# Until a provider is configured the form still works — it falls back to opening
# the visitor's mail client with the message pre-filled, so nothing is lost.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTION A — SMTP (works today, no domain needed)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Gmail requires an App Password, not your normal password:
#   1. Turn on 2-Step Verification: https://myaccount.google.com/signinoptions/two-step-verification
#   2. Create an App Password:      https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#   3. Paste the 16-character value below (spaces are fine to remove)
#
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=465
# SMTP_USER=ssentanmuseth@gmail.com
# SMTP_PASS=your-16-char-app-password


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTION B — Resend (preferred once Ektelo.com is registered)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sign up at https://resend.com, then API Keys → Create API Key (sending access).
#
# IMPORTANT: before you verify a domain, Resend only delivers to the address
# the account was created with. To reach both contact addresses you must add
# Ektelo.com under Domains, publish the SPF/DKIM records it gives you, and set
# CONTACT_FROM to an address at that domain.
#
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# CONTACT_FROM="Ektelo Website <engage@Ektelo.com>"


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional, applies to either provider
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated. Defaults to site.emails in src/lib/data.ts.
# CONTACT_TO=ssentanmuseth@gmail.com
